<Project Sdk="Aspire.AppHost.Sdk/13.0.0">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <UserSecretsId>vix-aspire-apphost</UserSecretsId>
    <!-- Nullable / ImplicitUsings / TreatWarningsAsErrors come from the root Directory.Build.props. -->
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Aspire.Hosting.AppHost" Version="13.6.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Aspire.Hosting.SqlServer" Version="13.6.0" />
    <!-- SECURITY PIN, not a used dependency: no source file in this project
         references MessagePack. Aspire.Hosting.* 13.0.0 -> StreamJsonRpc 2.22.23
         depends on MessagePack with a bare minimum of ">= 2.5.192", which carries
         11 advisories (9 moderate + 2 HIGH: GHSA-hv8m-jj95-wg3x /
         GHSA-vh6j-jc39-fggf). Aspire.Hosting.SqlServer is a *direct* reference, so
         overriding the transitive version here is clean. Because TreatWarningsAsErrors
         is repo-wide (Directory.Build.props), NuGet audit warnings on the transitive
         2.5.192 are hard build errors, so deleting this line breaks the build outright.
         DO NOT "clean up" this line as unused: it is load-bearing.

         Why 2.5.301 exactly: every advisory that reaches the 2.x line has
         "< 2.5.301" as its vulnerable ceiling, so 2.5.301 is the FIRST patched 2.x
         version, not an arbitrary choice. Newer clean 2.x builds exist (2.5.302 /
         2.5.303 / 2.5.305) but add no security value over 2.5.301, and MessagePack
         3.x (>= 3.1.7) is a major-version jump under StreamJsonRpc's feet. The pin
         sits at the security-optimal minimum; the "security-pins" dependabot group
         will propose any future bump.

         Reachability: MessagePack is absent from src/NewVixSmart.Web's graph and
         from the published web output, and .dockerignore excludes this project, so
         it is a local-dev-harness dependency only and never ships. Both HIGHs are
         also in paths this harness does not exercise (LZ4 decompression, and
         unbounded reader recursion on attacker-shaped input), so the practical risk
         is low - but the NU1902/NU1903 build gate makes the pin mandatory anyway.

         Upgrade path: Aspire.Hosting 13.6.0 now declares MessagePack 2.5.302 as a
         DIRECT dependency (upstream fixed the transitive floor). Bumping Aspire
         would therefore lift the floor to a clean version on its own, but 13.0.0 ->
         13.6.0 is six minor versions of the orchestration SDK and a far larger blast
         radius than this finding warrants, so it is deliberately not done here.
         First patched v2 line: docs/audit-round18-findings.md (R18-8); the DCP /
         dashboard MessagePack log channel was runtime-verified on 2.5.301 in
         docs/audit-round19-findings.md. Covered by the "security-pins" dependabot
         group in .github/dependabot.yml. Guarded by DependencyMessagePackPinTests. -->
    <PackageReference Include="MessagePack" Version="2.5.302" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../../src/NewVixSmart.Web/NewVixSmart.Web.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../Vix.ServiceDefaults/Vix.ServiceDefaults.csproj" IsAspireProjectResource="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
